## Why

openSUSE removes patent-encumbered codecs from ffmpeg, GStreamer and VLC. Its openh264 repo adds only H.264.
Packman Essentials added the missing codecs.

packman-nova is not a full copy of Packman Essentials. It builds only the codecs: full ffmpeg, x264, x265, libde265, fdk-aac, libheif,
and codec plugins for GStreamer, VLC, xine-lib and libquicktime. No drivers, firmware, DVD or Blu-ray decryption.
The sources are the same as Packman's. The signing key is our own.

## Migrating from Packman

Find the Packman repo alias with `zypper lr`, remove it with `sudo zypper rr <alias>`, then follow the install steps of your distro.
Step 3 moves your Packman codec packages to these builds.
Other Packman packages stay installed, but get no more updates. List them with `zypper packages --orphaned`.
